00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:04.800
Macaron.

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.410
Macaron is baked with hardened whipped meringue added with sugar and almond powder mixed together.

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:16.240
The inside is filled with cream or sweets made of jam.

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:20.020
The outside is crispy and the inside is yet refreshing.

00:23:20.020 --> 00:23:22.060
A gentle and sweet feeling, isn't it?

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:32.930
France

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:32.930
Italy

00:23:22.970 --> 00:23:27.520
Macaron is an European sweet originated in 16th century from Italy, brought over to France.

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:32.800
And then, varieties of Macaron were born due to many different techniques of France.

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:36.690
For example, "Nancy's Macaron" of Lorraine.

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:40.870
"Saint-Émilion" of Bordeaux.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:44.190
"Paris-style Macaron" of Paris.

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:48.910
The one common in Japan is Paris-style Macaron.

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:54.960
Macaron is also called one of the sweets belonging to France but born in Italy.

00:23:55.470 --> 00:23:59.870
